}{\plain \f1 \'a91993,5 Advanced Systems Consultants, Inc. (ASC)\par
}{\plain \f1 \tab \par
}{\plain \f1 Running on the PSION SIBO family of products, this software product provides "easy\_to\_use" PC\_like 
communications software for the HC, Series 3/3A, and the new Workabout.  Using the terminal 
emulation, you can connect to the outside world of PC host systems, Unix systems, BBS networks, 
Compuserve, or any RS\_232 asynchronous host.  Using the file transfers, you can upload or download 
files using full error\_checking protocols such as XMODEM or YMODEM to insure 100% data integrity.  
You can create "Scripts" for logging into host systems automatically.  Further, these same scripts can 
be used directly with ProComm+ 2.0 for testing and debugging! \par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \f1 A dialing directory is included so that you can easily have a database of names on file with telephone 
numbers and parameters for each dialing entry. The whole package is written in 'C' for extremely fast 
operation, total low\_level hardware control, and designed to use as little memory as possible to allow 
for programmer calls.  It supports all standard Psion serial interfaces including EXTECH, Dynasys, and 
Psion 3FAX modem.  All functions use a simple PC\_like hot\_key approach such as  the Psion key (lock) 
plus "H" key for "Help"; the dialing directory is "Psion + D", etc.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1\fs28 APPLICATIONS}{\plain \f1 :\par
}{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \b\f1  }{\plain \f1 can be used for remote dial\_in\_access to update databases, get messages or files, download 
or upload a current price list or inventory file, control RS\_232 devices, emulate a host  terminal, call 
BBS systems, and many more.  If you are writing code for a Psion terminal, you can call }{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \f1  
with a script file from OPL/G or 'C' for total communications control.  Write your applications in OPL/G 
or 'C', collect the data, and then pass control to }{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \f1  to dial host systems to upload all collected 
data.  \par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}\pard\page 
\pard \qj 
{\plain \b\f1\fs28 FEATURES:}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 TERMINAL EMULATION}{\plain \f1 :  PC\_ANSI, VT100, or  IBM 3270.  VT100 emulation can be used with 
many host mainframes.  ANSI would be used for PC mode emulations, and 3270 supports IBM 
mainframe: CICS, VTAM, and PROFS!, etc.  }{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \f1  supports screen control characters as well 
as function keys such as PF1, F1, etc.  Series 3A features a 25x80 screen, or, you can use our scrolling 
virtual window.  }{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \f1  was designed especially for small screen terminals.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 FILE TRANSFERS}{\plain \f1 :  Supports XMODEM, YMODEM (and YMODEM batch), and ASCII protocols.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 DIALING DIRECTORY}{\plain \f1 :  A database of names (limited only by disk space) includes telephone 
numbers, dialing parameters with port setups for each entry which also allows for multiple serial ports 
on your Psion HC terminal. Supports international dialing and most PBX systems.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 HAYES MODEM COMPATIBLE}{\plain \f1 :  Uses standard Hayes Modem commands, but you can choose 
your own modem initialization string.  Configuration file allows you to select 300\_19200 baud rates, 7 
or 8 data bits, l or 2 stop bits, ODD, EVEN, or NO parity, and Port A, B, Cradle, D, or E, etc.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 HOT KEYS}{\plain \f1 :  like the PC ALT  key, use the PSION(LOCK) key for fast execution on commands as 
well as ease of use.  Some more examples of Psion hot keys:\par
}{\plain \f1 (Utilizes least keystrokes possible.)\par
}\pard \qj\fi-6480\li6480\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480 
{\plain \f1 \tab (diamond) + 1 = F1/PF1 for IBM Hosts\tab \tab \tab (diamond) + 2 = F2/PF2\par
}\pard \qj\fi-6480\li6480\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480 
{\plain \f1 \tab PSION + S = Setup Configuration\tab \tab \tab \tab PSION + P = Port setup\par
}\pard \qj\fi-6480\li6480\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480 
{\plain \f1 \tab PSION + U = upload file\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab PSION + W = download file\par
}\pard \qj\fi-5760\li5760\tx5760 
{\plain \f1 \tab CTRL + (UP ARROW) = scroll up virtual window\tab \par
}\pard \qj 
{\plain \f1 \tab CTRL + (DN ARROW) = scroll down virtual window\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 SCRIPTING MODE}{\plain \f1 :  We consider this our most powerful feature as you can fully automate all of 
your communications with this.  You can execute the script by typing "PCOMM scriptname.ASP" where 
scriptname is a standard ASCII text file, or execute the script file from within }{\plain \b\f1 PCOMM}{\plain \b\sub\f1 (tm)}{\plain \b\f1  }{\plain \f1 with one 
hot\_key.  The script file also works directly with ProComm+ 2.0 (when compiled with ProComm+) 
which is great when used as a development tool.  Scripting can be used to automatically log into BBS 
systems using passwords, log into your own host systems for file transfers, check EMAIL, etc.  It's only 
limited by your creative imagination.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 MACRO KEYS}{\plain \f1 :  allow custom key mapping, special codes, even execute script files with this feature.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 3270 EMULATION}{\plain \f1 :  allows remote connection to an IBM mainframe such as a 3090 or ES9000 and 
you can run PROFS, CICS, VTAM, etc.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 DIAGNOSTICS MODE}{\plain \f1 :  allows visual verification of the line status for RTS, CTS, DSR, DTR, DCD 
as well as modification of DTR.\par
}{\plain \f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 SCREEN CAPTURE}{\plain \f1 :  allows screens to be captured to a file on your Psion computer.\par
}{\plain \b\f1 \par
}{\plain \b\f1 \par
